<h1>Security Model</h1>
<p class="subtitle">vexes processes untrusted package, advisory, registry, source, and configuration data. It reduces selected risks; it does not eliminate them.</p>

<h2>Trusted components and upstreams</h2>
<p>The Node.js runtime, built-in modules, vendored Acorn code, the vexes implementation, and the local operating environment remain trusted. OSV and registries are upstream evidence sources; their responses are still treated as untrusted input for parsing and display.</p>

<h2>Implemented mitigations</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Zero external runtime npm dependencies:</strong> reduces transitive install-time exposure. It does not remove runtime or vendored-code risk.</li>
  <li><strong>Terminal sanitization:</strong> shared output paths strip selected OSC/CSI/DCS/C0/C1 and escape forms. Complete coverage of every command-specific field is not claimed.</li>
  <li><strong>Config merging:</strong> rejects prototype-pollution keys. Project policy can still suppress ordinary evidence unless <code>--no-project-config</code> is used.</li>
  <li><strong>Guard command construction:</strong> narrow public-npm grammar and <code>execFileSync</code> argument arrays avoid a shell in that path.</li>
  <li><strong>Bounded archive handling:</strong> compressed/decompressed size limits, HTTPS and host restrictions, redirect limits, and tar-size validation reduce archive/SSRF/memory risk.</li>
  <li><strong>npm artifact metadata:</strong> static sampling checks registry SRI/shasum when present; dynamic extraction refuses missing digest metadata. The current PyPI sdist path is not digest-bound.</li>
  <li><strong>Fail-visible states:</strong> unsupported input shapes, requested network failures, and known coverage gaps are surfaced as incomplete rather than empty clean results.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Provenance boundary</h2>
<p>vexes decodes available npm provenance payloads and compares identity fields with package/repository metadata. It does not verify DSSE signatures, signing certificates, transparency-log inclusion, or every artifact digest. A present or internally consistent bundle is not a trust verdict.</p>

<h2>Static and dynamic analysis</h2>
<p>Default scan/analyze paths do not execute package code. <code>--deep</code> reads a bounded selected-file sample and is not exhaustive. The optional <code>--sandbox</code> path may execute one selected npm entrypoint under an accepted Linux <code>bwrap</code> layout. It does not run lifecycle hooks, does not execute PyPI packages, exposes selected runtime directories read-only, and records only a subset of Node APIs. The recorder is bypassable and not inherited by child processes. macOS execution is currently refused. Do not use it as a known-malware boundary.</p>

<h2>Guard boundary</h2>
<p>Guard constrains a narrow npm workflow and validates manifest/lockfile metadata. It does not independently verify installed bytes, cannot roll back all <code>node_modules</code> side effects, and cannot stop same-user races. It does not protect installs run without the explicit guard command.</p>

<h2>Network and data disclosure</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Scanning sends package coordinates to OSV.</li>
  <li>Analysis may contact npm/PyPI registries and provenance services, then download selected archives.</li>
  <li>License inventory may send coordinates to deps.dev.</li>
  <li>Opt-in AI features send bounded sanitized finding/advisory/import facts to the configured endpoint; package source files are not included in those explanation payloads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Known limits</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Advisories and registry metadata can be late, wrong, unavailable, or compromised.</li>
  <li>Static patterns miss runtime-only behavior, computed loading, child-process behavior, and unsampled files.</li>
  <li>Heuristics can both false-positive and false-negative.</li>
  <li>Name similarity uses a curated list and is not comprehensive typosquat detection.</li>
  <li>There has been no external security or efficacy audit.</li>
</ul>

<div class="warning-box"><strong>Exit 0 is deliberately narrow.</strong> It says requested supported checks completed with no finding at the active threshold. It does not certify dependency safety.</div>
